\begin{note}
\emph{3-way merge sort} is a variation of merge sort that splits
the input into three (roughly) equal pieces, recursively sorts
each piece, and then merges all three sorted lists together. The
recurrence is
\[
T(n) = 3 T(n/3) + O(n).
\]
Even though we are making more recursive calls, case 2 of the
master theorem still gives $T(n) = O(n \log n)$: the extra fan-out
is offset by the shorter recursion depth, and the total work at
every level of the recursion tree remains linear.
\end{note}
